<<!DOCTYPE type=`memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki` spec=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext`>>

<<^ code=`&#x0001;` from=`?` to=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/filters`>>
<<^ code=`&#x0002;`>>

```toml meta
cacheable = true
role      = "the house's named filters: the law index, the road state and the memory stage as canon functions; canon only"
tags      = ["$:/tags/Global", "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/filters"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/api/filters"
```

\function lares.law.pins()
[subfilter{$:/config/lares/law/pins}] :intersection[lares.law[]]
\end

\function lares.law()
[subfilter{$:/config/lares/law/pins}] =[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/]regexp[^lar:///ha\.ka\.ba/(\w|-)+/api/]!regexp[#]sort[title]] +[unique[]] :filter[regexp[^lar:///ha\.ka\.ba/(\w|-)+/api/]!regexp[#]] :filter[get[$origin-bag]regexp[^lar:///ha\.ka\.ba/bags/(oracle|lares|lararium)$]] :filter[regexp[^lar:///\S+$]]
\end

\function lares.road(state)
[tag[stage/road]] :filter[tags[]removeprefix[road/state/]match<state>]
\end

\function lares.stage(name)
[prefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]] :filter[<currentTiddler>removeprefix[lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/]removeprefix<name>removeprefix[/]]
\end

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The house's named filters

Four filters stand here as `\function` definitions, global to every filter the house runs: `[lares.law[]]` (the law index: the pins first, then every canon root meme under a bag's `api/` tree, each row answered from a canon layer), `[lares.law.pins[]]` (the pins that stand as canon law), `[lares.road[open]]` (the road memes whose `road/state/<state>` tag names the state) and `[lares.stage[state]]` (every title under `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/<stage>/`, slots too; `[lares.stage[state]!regexp[#]]` keeps the root memes). `lares wiki filter '[lares.law[]]'`, the wake and the MCP seat's `law_index` all run these same functions.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/names`>>

!! Why the names carry a period

TiddlyWiki resolves a user function as a filter operator only where its name holds a period (`filters/unknown.js`); a bare `law` would read as a field name. The `lares.` stem marks the house's own set.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/canon-only`>>

!! Canon only

A function the house names here comes from a canon layer alone. The daemon reads this carrier's text from the canon layers (the oracle floor and the system canon bags) and builds the functions from it; a tiddler a face writes into its working layer, one at this title or any other tagged `$:/tags/Global` that defines `lares.law`, `lares.road` or `lares.stage`, never changes what a filter answers. No seat redefines another's query.

<<~/ahu>>

